Subject: [PATCH] Deal finder for agents: the best fix and flips on the market,
 one press

/homes/deals/ (not in search; the DEALS_KEY password and a signed-up account, because it reads sold
homes). Fix and flip: homes for sale with a reason to be cheap (distressed sale, foreclosure, short
sale, older or lowest-priced houses), each valued from houses of about its size sold within a mile
(two if too few) in the last 12 months: the upper quarter of their price a square foot is the value
fixed up. Repairs start from the agent's own figures by age and distress; the AI then looks at the
photos and description of the best 12 (the analyzer's repair check and its saved answers) and
replaces them. Profit after buying, holding and selling, the return on the cash in, and the 70
percent rule's highest offer, with the sales behind each value. A price far below nearby sales is
marked to check. Long-term and short-term rentals are the next two buttons.

